      "content": "got it, that makes sense. so if you look at the two sides, it seems like the scientific arguments are built on these very concrete, data-driven goals like herd immunity and stopping outbreaks, whereas the civil liberties side is more about abstract rights and personal philosophy. do you think there's a way to easily reconcile those two, or is one side fundamentally more \"correct\" when it comes to actual public safety?",
