      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Reconciling these two perspectives often requires finding a balance between collective security and individual freedom, a difficult ethical tightrope walk. Many legal and ethical frameworks attempt to balance this by allowing limitations on rights when there is a compelling state interest, like preventing serious harm. Rather than one side being inherently \"more correct,\" the resolution usually involves setting the least restrictive means necessary to achieve a demonstrable public health benefit.",
